<section class="teaser-collection section-wrap collection--two-columns">
<div class="collection__items">
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Applied learning at Wichita State</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>At Wichita State, applied learning is everything. In fact, every degree we offer has a guaranteed applied learning or research experience built right into it equipping you with the relevant skills and experience to make you workforce ready before graduation.</p>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="{{d:3378519}}"> <span>Learn about our innovative approach</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Admission to the program</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>To qualify as a candidate for admission to the BSN program, students must meet the following requirements:</p>
<ul>
<li>Be enrolled in, or admitted to, WSU</li>
<li>Have completed prerequisite requirements</li>
<li>Have an overall minimum 2.75 GPA, and a 3.00 cumulative GPA in the specified science courses</li>
<li>Submit application materials by Jan. 15 for fall or Aug. 15 for spring</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="https://catalog.wichita.edu/undergraduate/health-professions/nursing/bachelor-science-nursing-traditional-program/#admissiontext"> <span>Admission requirements</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section-wrap section-wrap--dots"><header class="section-header section-header--no-border">
<h2>Inside the Program</h2>
</header>
<div class="teaser teaser--columned-intro">
<div class="teaser__image"><a> <img style="max-width: 115%; min-height: auto;" src="{{f:36443658}}" alt="Nursing students receive an interactive experience with state-of-the-art simulation mannequins in a realistic and safe environment." width="1400" height="1050" /></a></div>
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">State-of-the-art simulation technology prepares students for real-world nursing</span><span class="head"></span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>Our students gain hands-on, interactive experience using state-of-the-art simulation mannequins in a realistic and supportive environment.</p>
<p>These high-fidelity mannequins replicate a wide range of symptoms and scenarios, including childbirth, seizures, blood pressure fluctuations and bleeding &mdash; giving students the chance to practice critical skills before stepping into clinical settings.</p>
<p>Virtual Reality (VR) experiences immerse students in realistic healthcare environments and complex patient scenarios, strengthening clinical decision-making, communication, patient assessment skills and confidence.</p>
<p>Research shows that combining simulation with classroom learning and clinical practice helps better prepare future nurses and enhances patient safety.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section class="teaser-collection section-wrap collection--two-columns">
<div class="collection__items">
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Curriculum</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>A minimum total of 120 credit hours is required for the Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) and includes 60 credit hours of major (professional) courses.</p>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="http://catalog.wichita.edu/undergraduate/health-professions/nursing/bachelor-science-nursing-traditional-program/#requirementstext"> <span>View the curriculum</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="teaser collection__item ">
<div class="teaser__body">
<div class="teaser__headline">
<h3 class="headline-group "><span class="head">Careers</span></h3>
</div>
<div class="teaser__editorial">
<p>A nursing degree from Wichita State will give you the knowledge and practical skills for high-paying, high-demand nursing careers in diverse health care settings such as hospitals, nursing and residential care facilities, schools and government.</p>
</div>
<div class="teaser__links"><a class=" link--rich" href="https://www.bls.gov/ooh/healthcare/registered-nurses.htm#tab-1"> <span>Learn more about careers in this field</span> </a></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<table class="ou-snippet-generic-section"><caption><img class="snippet-preview" src="/_resources/images/snippet_previews/generic-section.png" alt="Use to contain other Snippets on landing pages and additional content areas" />Snippet: Generic Section</caption>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td data-select-list="backgrounds">section-wrap--wheat</td>
<td data-select-list="arrows">section-wrap--pointer-down</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td colspan="2">
<h3>Wichita State and Kansas State Pathway to Nursing Program</h3>
<p><span style="font-size: 18px;">The <strong><a title="Learn more about the Pathway to Nursing Program" href="{{f:34045592}}">Wichita State and Kansas State Pathway to Nursing Program</a></strong>&nbsp;is a unique dual degree program that gives students the opportunity to earn both a Bachelor of Science (BS) degree from the College of Health and Human Sciences at Kansas State and a Bachelor of Science in nursing (BSN) from the College of Health Professions at Wichita State University.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
